note The anchor a node button sets before its tree changes shape, from apply's ToggleCollapsed and Toggle arms: the node and its pixel position relative to the pan this frame. After the relayout move_camera shifts the pan by the node's displacement, so expanding or hiding its callees or callers, or cutting it to a preview, leaves it and the button under the pointer exactly where they were; the new nodes appear beside it and the reader pans if they run off the canvas.

